{
  "service": "IAM",
  "title": "IAM coverage",
  "page": "site/docs/reference/iam-coverage.md",
  "group": "Core",
  "console_service": "iam",
  "intro": [
    "Users, roles, policies, keys and identity providers, laid out like AWS's IAM",
    "console: a dashboard, the identity lists, account settings and the credential",
    "report. The IAM users page is the one place the console owns state of its own —",
    "it creates, deletes and re-passwords console principals over the control API.",
    "",
    "Everything else is the emulator's own API, run through the console catalogue;",
    "the generic API explorer at `/iam/home` still runs the actions the dedicated",
    "pages do not draw.",
    "",
    "`tests/control/test_iam_operations.py` drives every advertised operation through the",
    "emulator's own query protocol and reads the state back, so the test column has no gaps.",
    "The emulator also answers two group operations its README row omits — `ListGroups` and",
    "`DeleteGroup` — and the suite drives those too.",
    "The identity policies are enforced, not decoration: `tests/control/test_iam_policies.py`",
    "then runs a matrix of users with different policies against a live lab (it skips",
    "without one, because the in-process emulator runs with `AUTH` off)."
  ],
